# COMPLETE SETUP INSTRUCTIONS

## 1. Create the backend directory structure:
```bash
mkdir -p backend/{config,middleware,routes,models,controllers,services,utils,data,tests}
cd backend
```

## 2. Initialize the project:
```bash
npm init -y
```

## 3. Install dependencies:
```bash
npm install express express-rate-limit helmet cors bcryptjs jsonwebtoken mongoose redis joi dotenv compression express-mongo-sanitize express-validator winston nodemailer stripe multer sharp slug uuid
```

## 4. Install dev dependencies:
```bash
npm install -D nodemon jest supertest eslint
```

## 5. Create environment file:
```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

## 6. Edit .env file with your settings:
```bash
nano .env
```

## 7. Start MongoDB (if running locally):
```bash
# On Ubuntu/Debian:
sudo systemctl start mongod

# Or using Docker:
docker run -d -p 27017:27017 --name mongodb mongo:latest
```

## 8. Start Redis (optional, for caching):
```bash
# On Ubuntu/Debian:
sudo systemctl start redis-server

# Or using Docker:
docker run -d -p 6379:6379 --name redis redis:latest
```

## 9. Seed the database:
```bash
npm run seed
```

## 10. Start the development server:
```bash
npm run dev
```

## 11. Test the API:
```bash
# Test health endpoint
curl http://localhost:4000/health

# Test products endpoint
curl http://localhost:4000/v1/products

# Test categories endpoint
curl http://localhost:4000/v1/categories
```

## 12. Update your frontend .env file:
```bash
# In your frontend directory, update .env or .env.local:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000/v1
```

## For Production Deployment on Vercel:

### 1. Create vercel.json in backend root:
```json
{
  "version": 2,
  "builds": [
    {
      "src": "server.js",
      "use": "@vercel/node"
    }
  ],
  "routes": [
    {
      "src": "/(.*)",
      "dest": "/server.js"
    }
  ],
  "env": {
    "NODE_ENV": "production"
  }
}
```

### 2. Set environment variables in Vercel dashboard:
- MONGODB_URI (use MongoDB Atlas)
- JWT_SECRET
- REDIS_URL (use Redis Cloud)
- ALLOWED_ORIGINS (your frontend URL)

### 3. Deploy:
```bash
vercel --prod
```

## Database Setup Options:

### Local MongoDB:
```bash
# Install MongoDB Community Edition
# https://docs.mongodb.com/manual/installation/

# Start MongoDB
mongod --dbpath ./data/db
```

### MongoDB Atlas (Recommended for production):
1. Go to https://www.mongodb.com/atlas
2. Create a free cluster
3. Get connection string
4. Update MONGODB_URI in .env

### Local Redis (Optional):
```bash
# Install Redis
sudo apt-get install redis-server

# Start Redis
redis-server
```

### Redis Cloud (Recommended for production):
1. Go to https://redis.com/try-free/
2. Create free account
3. Get connection URL
4. Update REDIS_URL in .env